The `shouldSkip` function uses simple glob matching. `CHANGELOG*` and `HISTORY*` are glob patterns on the basename; `*.snap` matches any `.snap` file. I need to verify `shouldSkip` handles glob patterns on basenames (not just full paths). Looking at the code — it already handles the `*` wildcard via regex. Let me trace through `CHANGELOG*`:

The pattern `CHANGELOG*` has no `/` and has `*` → goes to the glob branch → `escaped = 'CHANGELOG[^/]*'` → regex `(^|/)CHANGELOG[^/]*(/|$)`. That matches `CHANGELOG.md`, `CHANGELOG` etc. Good.

